.TH CLOG_GET_LEVEL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clog_get_level \- return the current minimum log level
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clogger.h>

clog_level_t clog_get_level(clog logger);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the current minimum severity level of the logger.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
logger  Logger handle.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Current minimum level.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Thread-safe.  The minimum level is an atomic value that belongs to each
logger.  It is separate from the lock that serialises the writes and
the rotation for the shared output target.  A read of the level of one
logger therefore never contends with a write in progress on a sibling
logger that shares the same target.
Asserts when logger is CLOG_INVALID, stale or already closed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_set_level (3)
